## 12. What would kill it

**The live one:** a system with subjective awareness and no symmetric channel *anywhere* in the nesting. Not just no corpus callosum — none at any scale.

**A second I can state but not run:** both channels closed, capacity adequate, and no awareness. That needs a way to detect phenomenality independent of the architecture, and nobody has one. Until then it's inert, because any apparent failure could be blamed on some further condition I forgot.

**One that would wound without killing:** show that channel discriminability comes apart from level of awareness across a range of perturbations.

**And one aimed at §9 specifically.** The grounded/facilitated distinction arrived in response to a case that broke an earlier claim, which is exactly the shape of a rescue. It survives only if it does work elsewhere — deriving Goodhart, predicting institutional decay from self-written constraint, restructuring the engineered-systems list. If it turns out to do nothing outside the corporation case, it's a save and it goes.

---

## 13. Still open

The honest list is long. The ones that would change the shape of the thing:

- Three conditions (temporal unification, self-modeling, valence) are treated as on/off by scoping decision. They all admit of degree and nobody has graded them.
- Constraint efficacy is stated and not measured. I know what the asymmetric limb has to do; I can't yet put a number on whether it's doing it.
- Discriminability is measured against a background the channel may have shaped over time — so a channel can capture its own baseline and then look like it's clearing it.
- Does the identity tier have an error signal of its own? Right now nothing lets a life story be *wrong* in a way the system registers, which is what fracture and misattribution seem to need. First question to settle: whether it just reduces to anticipated homeostatic error, in which case it isn't a second signal at all.
- Sufficiency. Everything here is necessary conditions. What closes the gap is unaddressed.

---

## The whole thing in one breath

Split a system in two so it can represent itself. Give one of the crossings a format change so it touches something outside. Make sure both crossings actually carry — not just exist. That gets you a subject. Add other subjects to compare against and you get a self. Let the system write its own constraints and you get something that looks like all of the above and isn't.

